# Modular Design

- Single Responsibility: if a function needs "and" to describe it, split it.
- Keep functions under ~40 lines and files under ~300 lines. Propose a refactor before adding more.
- Depend on abstractions, not implementations. Business logic never imports UI. Isolate data access behind a repository/service layer.
- Organize by feature, not by type (`features/vehicles/` with components, hooks, services — not global `utils/` dumping grounds).
- No circular dependencies. If two modules need each other, extract shared logic into a third.
- Prefer composition over inheritance. Max 1 inheritance level.
- Extract magic numbers and repeated strings into named constants.
- Before duplicating logic a third time, extract a shared utility (rule of three).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — mixed concerns, type-based dump
// src/utils/helpers.ts + src/components/VehicleStuff.tsx
export function loadAndFormatVehicles() { /* fetch + UI mapping */ }

// ✅ GOOD — feature module, one job each
// features/vehicles/services/vehicle-repository.ts
export async function getVehicles(): Promise<Vehicle[]> { /* data only */ }

// features/vehicles/lib/format-vehicle.ts
export function formatVehicleLabel(vehicle: Vehicle): string { /* mapping only */ }
```
